> The network actually fitted

The following single-row shape probe executes the full 784–32–784 sigmoid network. Flow style
and layer detail are explicit. This is a reconstruction-path diagram; the preceding method figure
shows the additional scalar penalty branch. Its 50,992 learned scalars have the same names and
layout as the original source. Spatial and channel/vector shape scales are linear, with a two-pixel
visibility floor and at most six sampled shape planes. The flow glyphs aggregate whole tensors;
they do not depict 784 individual pixels. Exact tensor shapes remain in labels and tooltips.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/contractive_architecture.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  n::ParameterStore p(1753);
  n::Module model([&](const n::Tensor& input) {
    return n::models::ContractiveAutoencoder(p, input, .01).reconstruction;
  }, "Contractive autoencoder: 784 to 32 sigmoid to 784");
  n::ModelPlotOptions options;
  options.style = n::ModelPlotStyle::Flow;
  options.detail = n::ModelPlotDetail::Layers;
  options.sizing.spatial_scale = n::ModelPlotScale::Linear;
  options.sizing.channel_scale = n::ModelPlotScale::Linear;
  options.sizing.minimum_extent = 2;
  options.sizing.max_planes = 6;
  const auto figure = model.plot(n::zeros({1, 784}), options);
  if (p.count() != 50992 || figure.parameter_count() != p.count()) return 1;
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  figure.save_svg("build/contractive_architecture.svg");
  std::print("{} learned tensors, {} learned scalars.\n", p.size(), p.count());
}
```
